Step 1: Prove true for n=1
when n=1,
LHS = \dfrac{1}{3^{1}} = \dfrac{1}{3}        RHS = \dfrac{3^{1} - 1}{2 \times 3^{1}} = \dfrac{2}{6} = \dfrac{1}{3}
∴ true for n=1
Step 2: Let n=k be a number for which the statement is true
i.e. \dfrac{1}{3} + \dfrac{1}{9} + \dfrac{1}{27} + \dots + \dfrac{1}{3^{k}} = \dfrac{3^{k} - 1}{2(3^{k})}
